-- title:
--   Origin chart is dense in T[[X]] modulo (mathfrak m_T,X)ⁿ
-- statement:
--   Let $T$ be a commutative local ring and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$, and let `OriginChartRing W` denote the degree-zero part of the homogeneous localization, away from the second projective coordinate $Y$, of the graded ring $T[X,Y,Z]$ modulo the ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of the projective model of $W$ (the grading being the one induced on the quotient from the homogeneous components of $T[X,Y,Z]$). Let $\Phi : \mathcal O(D_+(Y)) \to T[[X]]$ be a ring homomorphism subject to three normalisations: for every $t \in T$, $\Phi$ of the image of $t$ under the structure map of $T$ into the degree-zero piece, viewed in the origin chart, is the constant series $C(t)$; $\Phi(X/Y) = -X$; and $\Phi(Z/Y) = -w$, where $w$ is the formal $w$-series of $W$ assembled from the iterates of the Weierstrass substitution by $w = \mathrm{mk}\,(n \mapsto \mathrm{coeff}_n(\mathrm{wIter}\,n))$. Then for every $n \in \mathbb N$ and every $b \in T[[X]]$ there is $a$ in the origin chart ring with $b - \Phi(a) \in \mathfrak m^n$, where $\mathfrak m = (\mathfrak m_T, X)$ is the maximal ideal of the local ring $T[[X]]$.
--
--   This is the density (approximate surjectivity) half of the statement that $T[[X]]$ is the completion of the origin chart of the projective Weierstrass model along the ideal cutting out the origin section. It is used in the construction of a ring homomorphism from the origin chart localised at the relevant prime into $T[[X]]$ with a faithful flatness property, in [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.exists_ringHom_localization_atPrime_powerSeries_comp_eq_and_faithfullyFlat`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.exists_ringHom_localization_atPrime_powerSeries_comp_eq_and_faithfullyFlat).
